  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Guardrail contract (ADR-0004/0017)",
      "items": [
        "Gap Analysis Agent retries Notice Corpus/EDM timeouts with backoff internally (ADR-0018) — a timeout is never treated as \"no matching clause\"; only a real absence of a grounded citation reaches Human Review Flags",
        "\"Human Review Flags\" merges two distinct logged reasons — insufficient_grounding (ADR-0004) and low-confidence supersession (decision 30) — both route to the same Examiner Dashboard queue but are logged distinctly in audit_log"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Tool calls (not drawn — see agent-specifications.md)",
      "items": [
        "Gap Analysis Agent calls notice_corpus.get_clause(), edm.query(), and supersession_graph.check() inside this node — full tool contracts, retry policy, and timeout values live in agent-specifications.md / ADR-0018, not duplicated here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "How to read this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Branch points (e.g. Gap Analysis's grounded/ungrounded split) are edge-labeled, not drawn as decision diamonds — archify's workflow grammar has no decision-node/fork-join primitive, so guard conditions live on the edge label, not a gateway shape",
        "Closest standard: a UML activity diagram without gateway notation. Human checkpoints use a dedicated lane, not a person-icon convention"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
